at:Evidence ;
rdfs:label "Padova 19 febbraio 1946 Si è costituita in questi giorni la 'FAMIGLIA ARTISTICA PADOVANA' composta di artisti e amatori dell'arte"@it ;
rdfs:label "Padua, February 19, 1946. The 'PADOVAN ARTISTIC FAMILY', composed of artists and art lovers, was formed in recent days"@en .

:1a8f54a9-9c0b-43b6-8174-83bdaa5af4d0
rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
at:Source ;
rdfs:label "FAMIGLIA DEGLI ARTISTI PADOVANI: Statuto"@it ;
rdfs:comment "Statute of the Padovan Artistic Family (FAP) that defines the organisation's objectives and activities"@en ;
dcterms:identifier "man_-mio_0004_0002_0001_0004"@it .

:8f6fc9af-087c-426e-8fc5-746f7221d231
rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
at:InterpretiveObservation ;
rdfs:label "The FAP appears to promote the integration of art into architecture, including industrial buildings"@en ;
rdfs:comment "The analysis of the Statute of the Padovan Artistic Family (FAP) suggests a strong interest in promoting art as a civic value and in recognising the role of craftsmanship. The statute explicitly encourages the integration of works of art into public, private and industrial buildings. This cultural context suggests that the environment in which Mansutti operated did not necessarily regard modernisation and figurative art as mutually exclusive, making the incorporation of artistic elements, such as the frescoes of the First IRE Building, plausible within an industrialised architectural project."@en .

