at:Evidence ;
rdfs:label "Carlo Rossi's concept of Unification"@en ;
rdfs:comment "Carlo Rossi's concept of Unification"@en .

:07dca2d9-d1c1-4bc8-b001-d96768b17817
rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
at:Source ;
rdfs:label "Letter from Francesco Mansutti to Carlo Rossi on Reconstruction"@en ;
dcterms:identifier "man_-mio_0004_0005_0006_0074"@it .

:619b9f46-3471-43e1-a301-c1a950521dfa
rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
at:Evidence ;
rdfs:label "[…] è necessario, perché è doveroso far conoscere ai padovani la loro città far loro sapere che Padova è una delle gemme d’Italia anche se nessuno lo sa, anche se molti fingono di ignorarlo e vi esaltano p. es. Siena e Perugia ed Orvieto ecc. ecc. alle quali Padova non ha assolutamente nulla da invidiare anche se ha perso gran parte di quel meraviglioso momento d’arte che era costituito dagli affreschi della Cappella Ovetari del Mantegna. Agli increduli io cito solo queste diverse e differenti testimonianze: Scrovegni, Gattamelata, basilica del Santo, Salone [...] E per tornare al tema della modestia patavina voi potete arrivare […] a vedere p. es. che il Salone, noto sì per la unicità della mole ma collocato nei posti di secondo ordine rispetto al Salone palladiano è invece di tanto più grandioso, più vivo, più potente"@it ;
rdfs:label "[…] it is necessary, because it is our duty to let the Paduans know about their city, to let them know that Padua is one of the gems of Italy even if no one knows it, even if many pretend to ignore it and praise, for example, Siena and Perugia and Orvieto, etc., etc., which Padua has absolutely nothing to envy even if it has lost much of that marvelous moment of art that was constituted by the frescoes of the Ovetari Chapel by Mantegna. To the incredulous, I cite only these various and different testimonies: Scrovegni, Gattamelata, Basilica del Santo, Salone [...] And to return to the theme of Paduan modesty, you can get […] to see, for example, that the Salone, known for its unique size but located in the second tier compared to the Palladian Salone, is instead much more grandiose, more lively, more powerful"@en .

:b8bf9e40-6511-4e00-a050-c93fda412800
rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
at:Hypothesis ;
rdfs:label "Mansutti's use of Padua's historic monuments as cultural references"@en ;
rdfs:comment "Hypothesis suggesting that Mansutti may have adopted Padua's historic monuments as iconographic or cultural references to integrate modern architecture into the historic urban fabric."@en .

:3e1e5944-a738-4c44-b59d-57a53cf190ab
rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
at:CorrelationActivity ;
rdfs:label "Correlation of Interpretive Observations from Carlo Rossi's Book and Mansutti's Letter"@en ;
rdfs:comment "Correlation of interpretive observations derived from Carlo Rossi's book Unification and Mansutti's letter to identify a possible shared broad and forward-looking vision of reconstruction"@en .

